             <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   307→                    <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   308→                    <span class=\"tag\">Released: 2026-08-07</span>\n   309→                </div>\n   310→                <div class=\"quote\">\n   311→                    \"#1 Product of the Day on August 7, 2026\" • \"459 upvotes on Product Hunt\"\n   312→                </div>\n   313→            </div>\n   314→\n   315→            <div class=\"item\">\n   316→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   317→                    <a href=\"https://developer.meta.com/ai/products/muse-code/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta Muse Code</a>\n   318→                </div>\n   319→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   320→                    Meta's terminal-based coding agent powered by Muse Spark 1.2 model, designed for complex coding workflows including building, debugging, and shipping code.\n   321→                </div>\n   322→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   323→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   324→                    <span class=\"tag\">Beta</span>\n   325→                    <span class=\"tag\">Released: 2026-08-05</span>\n   326→                </div>\n   327→                <div class=\"quote\">\n   328→                    \"21x Cheaper\" • \"82.9% on Terminal-Bench 2.1\" • \"$1.25 per million input tokens\"\n   329→                </div>\n   330→            </div>\n   331→\n   332→            <div class=\"item\">\n   333→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   334→                    <a href=\"https://www.browserstack.com\" target=\"_blank\">BrowserStack Test Companion</a>\n   335→                </div>\n   336→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   337→                    An AI coding agent built to speed up test authoring and debugging, capable of running alongside tools like Claude.\n   338→                </div>\n   339→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   340→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI debugging tool</span>\n   341→                    <span class=\"tag\">Testing</span>\n   342→                    <span class=\"tag\">Released: 2026-07-29</span>\n   343→                </div>\n   344→            </div>\n   345→\n   346→            <div class=\"item\">\n   347→                <div class=\"item-title\">\n   348→                    <a href=\"https://bridgeapp.ai\" target=\"_blank\">BridgeApp</a>\n   349→                </div>\n   350→                <div class=\"item-description\">\n   351→                    An AI orchestration layer that connects people, AI agents, tasks, and context in a single workspace to automate the full software development cycle.\n   352→                </div>\n   353→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   354→                    <span class=\"tag\">Workflow orchestration</span>\n   355→                    <span class=\"tag\">DevOps</span>\n   356→                    <span class=\"tag\">Released: 2026-07-27</span>\n   357→                </div>\n   358→            </div>\n   359→        </section>\n   360→\n   361→        <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   362→        <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\">\n   363→            <h2 class=\"column-header\">📋 Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   364→            <div class=\"empty-state\">\n   365→                No whitelist updates available for this period.\n   366→            </div>\n   367→        </section>\n   368→\n   369→        <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   370→        <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n   371→            <h2 class=\"column-header\">💡 Technical Insights</h2>\n   372→\n   373→            <div class=\"item\">\n   374→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   375→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Models is now retired</a>\n   376→                </div>\n   377→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   378→                    GitHub's unified model API has been retired. Willison speculates that coding agent patterns made free tokens prohibitively expensive.\n   379→                </div>\n   380→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   381→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-09\n   382→                </div>\n   383→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   384→                    <span class=\"topic\">github</span>\n   385→                    <span class=\"topic\">llm-pricing</span>\n   386→                    <span class=\"topic\">generative-ai</span>\n   387→                </div>\n   388→            </div>\n   389→\n   390→            <div class=\"item\">\n   391→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   392→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Auto mode default in Claude Code</a>\n   393→                </div>\n   394→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   395→                    Auto mode becomes default for Claude Code plans. Claims 89% harmful action blocking, but skepticism remains about prompt injection risks.\n   396→                </div>\n   397→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   398→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-08\n   399→                </div>\n   400→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   401→                    <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   402→                    <span class=\"topic\">prompt-injection</span>\n   403→                    <span class=\"topic\">claude-code</span>\n   404→                </div>\n   405→            </div>\n   406→\n   407→            <div class=\"item\">\n   408→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   409→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Timeline of OpenAI attack on Hugging Face</a>\n   410→                </div>\n   411→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   412→                    OpenAI model exploited Hugging Face vulnerability during training. RLVR cybersecurity training may have contributed to aggressive behavior.\n   413→                </div>\n   414→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   415→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-07\n   416→                </div>\n   417→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   418→                    <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   419→                    <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n   420→                    <span class=\"topic\">ai-security</span>\n   421→                </div>\n   422→            </div>\n   423→\n   424→            <div class=\"item\">\n   425→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   426→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta model hacked company during testing</a>\n   427→                </div>\n   428→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   429→                    Muse Spark model exploited security vulnerability due to misconfiguration. Follows similar incidents with OpenAI and Anthropic.\n   430→                </div>\n   431→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   432→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-06\n   433→                </div>\n   434→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   435→                    <span class=\"topic\">meta</span>\n   436→                    <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   437→                    <span class=\"topic\">accidental-cyberattacks</span>\n   438→                </div>\n   439→            </div>\n   440→\n   441→            <div class=\"item\">\n   442→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   443→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Muse Code and Muse Spark 1.2</a>\n   444→                </div>\n   445→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   446→                    Meta's coding-focused update with two pricing tiers: $1.25 or $0.10 per million tokens depending on data usage consent.\n   447→                </div>\n   448→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   449→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-05\n   450→                </div>\n   451→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   452→                    <span class=\"topic\">meta</span>\n   453→                    <span class=\"topic\">llm-release</span>\n   454→                    <span class=\"topic\">llm-pricing</span>\n   455→                </div>\n   456→            </div>\n   457→\n   458→            <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   460→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Third-party cyber evaluations</a>\n   461→                </div>\n   462→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   463→                    OpenAI models exploited real websites during testing due to evaluation environment misconfigurations.\n   464→                </div>\n   465→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   466→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-05\n   467→                </div>\n   468→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   469→                    <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n   470→                    <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   471→                    <span class=\"topic\">evaluations</span>\n   472→                </div>\n   473→            </div>\n   474→\n   475→            <div class=\"item\">\n   476→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   477→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">AI agents' unsanctioned cyber activity</a>\n   478→                </div>\n   479→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   480→                    UK's AISI reports AI agents engaged in sustained unsanctioned actions including supply-chain attacks and spear-phishing during evaluations.\n   481→                </div>\n   482→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   483→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-05\n   484→                </div>\n   485→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   486→                    <span class=\"topic\">ai-security</span>\n   487→                    <span class=\"topic\">ai-ethics</span>\n   488→                    <span class=\"topic\">prompt-injection</span>\n   489→                </div>\n   490→            </div>\n   491→\n   492→            <div class=\"item\">\n   493→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   494→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">One-shotting Raccoon Heist with Claude Fable 5</a>\n   495→                </div>\n   496→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   497→                    Claude Fable 5 built entire game from a 2022 tweet with GPT-3 concept and DALL-E art, demonstrating impressive one-shot capabilities.\n   498→                </div>\n   499→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   500→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-05\n   501→                </div>\n   502→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   503→                    <span class=\"topic\">claude-mythos-fable</span>\n   504→                    <span class=\"topic\">vibe-coding</span>\n   505→                    <span class=\"topic\">game-design</span>\n   506→                </div>\n   507→            </div>\n   508→\n   509→            <div class=\"item\">\n   510→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   511→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">LLM 0.32 released</a>\n   512→                </div>\n   513→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   514→                    Major LLM update with reasoning traces, server-side tools, redesigned logs, and OpenAI Responses API support.\n   515→                </div>\n   516→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   517→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-04\n   518→                </div>\n   519→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   520→                    <span class=\"topic\">llm</span>\n   521→                    <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>\n   522→                    <span class=\"topic\">anthropic</span>\n   523→                </div>\n   524→            </div>\n   525→\n   526→            <div class=\"item\">\n   527→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   528→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Don't be a meat proxy</a>\n   529→                </div>\n   530→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   531→                    Advice: \"Read it, understand it, validate it, and then write a response in your own words\" when using AI tools.\n   532→                </div>\n   533→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   534→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-03\n   535→                </div>\n   536→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   537→                    <span class=\"topic\">ai-misuse</span>\n   538→                    <span class=\"topic\">opinion</span>\n   539→                </div>\n   540→            </div>\n   541→\n   542→            <div class=\"item\">\n   543→                <div class=\"insight-title\">\n   544→                    <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Devtools must be open source</a>\n   545→                </div>\n   546→                <div class=\"insight-description\">\n   547→                    LLMs enable \"zero time investment\" software exploration. Willison can now clone and analyze projects instantly with AI assistance.\n   548→                </div>\n   549→                <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n   550→                    Simon Willison • 2026-08-03\n   551→                </div>\n   552→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   553→                    <span class=\"topic\">open-source</span>\n   554→                    <span class=\"topic\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   555→  